WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.963 --> 00:00:14.985
Time passed, and Ellen grew up.

2
00:00:16.826 --> 00:00:19.328
She got used to keeping rocks in her pockets.

3
00:00:19.828 --> 00:00:21.509
This kept her from floating away.

4
00:00:23.791 --> 00:00:27.273
And her parents began to enjoy having a light princess.

5
00:00:27.914 --> 00:00:31.116
With Ellen, the palace always rang with laughter.

6
00:00:31.736 --> 00:00:33.277
Life was always fun!

7
00:00:37.561 --> 00:00:41.444
By the time Ellen was 17, her parents were uneasy again.

8
00:00:42.545 --> 00:00:45.307
Yes, Ellen delighted everyone with her laughter.

9
00:00:45.948 --> 00:00:50.151
But she laughed at everything—even things that were not funny.

10
00:00:52.132 --> 00:00:56.076
For instance, whenever the queen cried, Ellen giggled.

11
00:00:56.556 --> 00:01:01.180
"Hee-hee! Mama, you're squeezing water out of your cheeks again!"

12
00:01:04.273 --> 00:01:09.156
Whenever the king yelled, Ellen floated around him like a butterfly, grinning.

13
00:01:09.176 --> 00:01:13.779
"Make that mean face again, Papa!

14
00:01:14.419 --> 00:01:15.680
You look silly!"

15
00:01:17.981 --> 00:01:20.463
Then one day something awkward happened.

16
00:01:20.923 --> 00:01:23.524
Ellen was crossing the lawn with two servants.

17
00:01:24.445 --> 00:01:26.046
They held her hands tightly.

18
00:01:28.107 --> 00:01:32.173
But when Ellen saw her father, she yanked one hand away.

19
00:01:32.193 --> 00:01:39.078
"Papa!" Ellen looked for rocks to put in her pockets.

20
00:01:39.478 --> 00:01:42.580
But all she saw was a big black toad.

21
00:01:42.921 --> 00:01:44.642
She grabbed it and started running.

22
00:01:48.264 --> 00:01:51.206
She held out her arms, ready to kiss her father.

23
00:01:51.626 --> 00:01:53.528
Suddenly there was a puff of wind.

24
00:01:53.928 --> 00:01:58.311
The princess flew in another direction—into a young page's arms.

25
00:01:58.851 --> 00:02:04.889
Smack! The princess planted a kiss on one of the page's cheeks.

26
00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:10.311
On the other cheek, she slapped him—with the huge black toad!

27
00:02:11.351 --> 00:02:12.352
The princess giggled.

28
00:02:12.372 --> 00:02:15.713
"I hope you like toads!"

29
00:02:17.073 --> 00:02:20.194
The king turned red as she shrieked with laughter.

30
00:02:20.214 --> 00:02:22.955
"This is so embarrassing!"

31
00:02:23.275 --> 00:02:23.755
he thought.

32
00:02:23.775 --> 00:02:25.616
"Something must be done."

33
00:02:28.416 --> 00:02:31.337
The next morning the king and queen sent for the princess.

34
00:02:32.478 --> 00:02:35.239
She had only a few small stones in her pockets.

35
00:02:35.839 --> 00:02:38.240
So it took her a while to sit down.

36
00:02:41.842 --> 00:02:43.122
The king cleared his throat.

37
00:02:43.142 --> 00:02:47.424
"Ellen, you know you're different from everyone."

38
00:02:47.444 --> 00:02:49.845
"No, I'm not!"

39
00:02:51.105 --> 00:02:51.886
Ellen laughed.

40
00:02:51.906 --> 00:02:57.588
"I have a nose, two eyes, and a mouth, like everyone else."

41
00:02:59.116 --> 00:03:01.437
"Be serious," her mother said.

42
00:03:01.457 --> 00:03:03.819
"No, thank you.

43
00:03:04.179 --> 00:03:05.940
I like being silly!"

44
00:03:11.443 --> 00:03:12.984
Ellen laughed and laughed.

45
00:03:14.304 --> 00:03:15.645
The king looked at his wife.

46
00:03:15.665 --> 00:03:17.246
"Now what?"

47
00:03:17.266 --> 00:03:21.028
"There's only one thing to do," she said.

48
00:03:21.048 --> 00:03:27.091
"We must send for Kopp and Humm—the kingdom's wisest philosophers."
